course: dictionary
lesson: 777
title: Beautiful: pleasant to see and kind
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Beautiful means very pleasant to look at, hear or experience. Check the words around it: «Kintsugi is a Japanese art of mending broken pottery with gold, showing that cracks can be beautiful.» Mending pottery with gold and calling the cracks beautiful tells you the word means pleasing to see, even when something is broken.
explain: Beautiful can also mean very good or kind. In «It was beautiful of you to share your lunch», the word is about what you did, not how something looks. Try your meaning in the sentence: "It was very kind of you to share your lunch." It still makes sense, so the meaning fits.
explain: Beautiful often goes with words like day, music or place: «a beautiful day», «beautiful music». Ask yourself what the thing is like, and the meaning usually becomes clear.
fact: Beautiful is an adjective: beautiful, more beautiful, most beautiful.
fact: «Beautiful» means very pleasant to look at, hear or experience.
fact: «Beautiful» can also mean very good or kind, as in a beautiful thing to do.
fact: «Beau» means beautiful or handsome in French, but «il fait beau» means the weather is sunny and nice.
fact: Writers often pick a stronger or more exact word, such as stunning, lovely or graceful, to show the feeling they want.
exercise: «A gemstone is a mineral that is beautiful, rare and hard enough to cut and polish.» What does beautiful mean here? | Very loud | Broken into pieces | *Very pleasant to look at | Made of wood
exercise: Mia says, «It was beautiful of you to help Sam carry his bags.» What does beautiful mean in her sentence? | Very loud | *Very kind | Very heavy | Very far away
exercise: Which word could replace beautiful in «a beautiful day» without changing the meaning much? | quiet | broken | heavy | *lovely
test: In «showing that cracks can be beautiful», what is the beautiful thing? | *The cracks, mended with gold | The gold was stolen | The pottery was brand new | The cracks were hidden away
test: Which sentence uses beautiful to mean very kind? | The soup was rich and green. | The sky was beautiful at sunset. | The tureen was hot. | *It was beautiful of you to share your lunch.
exam: Which word fits best in «The sunset over the sea was ___»? | broken | heavy | *beautiful | quietly
